messages:
Maya: Postmortem follow-up: streaming/chat reliability remains a repeating problem. Root causes are a mix of long partial frames, intermittent ECONNRESET between gateway and runtime, and clients timing out. Need concrete owners for short and medium-term remediation.

Ethan: I can own SDK reconnect/resume behavior. Plan: add a conservative 3-attempt capped retry for transient errors, expose opt-in 'resume' flag for idempotent flows, and include a resume-token header so server can continue from last token. Target PR: 2026-04-07.

Rina: I'll take the runtime/server side. Short-term: increase internal keepalive to 10s, implement a partial_frame_detect metric, and add an API trailing partial frame: {"type":"partial_end","req":"<id>","cursor":"<c>"}. Design note by 2026-03-29.

Oliver: I'll handle monitoring and ops runbook. New metrics to add: partial_frame_count, resume_attempts, resume_success_rate, and avg_restart_latency. Alert if partial_frame_count > 50 in 10m or resume_success_rate < 90% in 30m. Runbook will include toggling SERVER_SMALL_CHUNKS and reducing gateway client timeout from 45s to 30s. Runbook draft by 2026-03-26.

Maya: Short-term mitigations to roll today: client retry for ECONNRESET/499, gateway timeout reduction, and runtime small-chunk mode behind feature flag. Rina, can you add SERVER_SMALL_CHUNKS toggle?

Rina: Yes. We will add SERVER_SMALL_CHUNKS with per-region toggles and a debug log emitted when toggled. Also introducing partial_frame_duration_ms to correlate with user-facing timeouts.

Ethan: Example pseudocode for client retry/resume:
```
if (stream.closed && err in [ECONNRESET, TIMEOUT, 499]) {
  for (i=1; i<=3; i++) {
    await sleep(expBackoff(i) + jitter());
    connect(headers={Resume-Token: lastToken});
    if (resumed) return;
  }
  fail();
}
```

Maya: Ownership recap: Ethan=SDK retries+resume (PR 2026-04-07), Rina=server partial-frame + keepalive + SERVER_SMALL_CHUNKS (design 2026-03-29), Oliver=monitoring, runbook, synthetics (2026-03-26). I'll coordinate customer comms and the postmortem update.

Oliver: Creating JIRA epic RT-4450 and subtasks. Will post links when created.

InfraBot: Epic RT-4450 created: "Streaming reliability remediations: resume, partial frames, ops mitigations". Creator: Oliver.

Ethan: I'll add integration tests simulating partial frames and ECONNRESET to ensure resume behavior is reliable. Test plan: simulate server closing after N tokens, assert client reconnect + resume receives remainder.

Rina: We should also return an explicit error code when the server aborts the stream with no resume possible. That helps clients surface a clear retry/no-retry decision.

Maya: Agreed. Add that to API changelog. Also, include compatibility notes for older SDKs and recommend customers upgrade or enable a temporary client-side flag.

Oliver: Will add dashboard panels and a weekly incident-pattern check to surface recurring trends to the postmortem board.

Maya: Let's aim to close short-term mitigations within 1 week and medium-term protocol changes within 6 weeks. I'll follow up with a sync next Tue to review progress. If blockers appear, post here and I'll escalate. Closing thread until next sync. :white_check_mark:
